  const levelBalancedPass = [["vocabulary","A1","Which word means “very small”?",["tiny","huge","heavy","wide"],0,"Tiny means very small.","Tiny تعني صغيرًا جدًا."],["spelling","A1","Choose the correctly spelled word.",["because","becuase","beacause","becaus"],0,"Because is the correct spelling.","Because هي التهجئة الصحيحة."],["grammar","A1","He ___ two sisters.",["has","have","having","is have"],0,"Use has with he, she, and it in the present simple.","نستخدم has مع he وshe وit في المضارع البسيط."],["story","A1","Lina sees dark clouds and takes an umbrella before leaving. Why?",["She thinks it may rain.","She wants to go swimming.","She is going to bed.","She has lost her shoes."],0,"Dark clouds suggest rain, so the umbrella is a sensible choice.","الغيوم الداكنة تشير إلى احتمال المطر، لذلك أخذ المظلة منطقي."],["listening","A1","“Sorry, I’m late. The bus didn’t come on time.” Why is the speaker late?",["The bus was delayed.","The speaker forgot the address.","The meeting was cancelled.","The speaker missed lunch."],0,"The speaker explains the delay by saying the bus was not on time.","يفسر المتحدث تأخره بأن الحافلة لم تصل في موعدها."],["advanced","A1","Choose the best reply to “Thank you for your help.”",["You’re welcome.","I’m ten years old.","It’s on the table.","Good night yesterday."],0,"“You’re welcome” is a natural response to thanks.","عبارة You’re welcome رد طبيعي على الشكر."],["vocabulary","A2","If you “lend” someone a book, you ___.",["let them use it and expect it back","buy it from them","throw it away","read it aloud only"],0,"Lend means to give something temporarily for another person to use.","Lend تعني إعطاء شيء لشخص ليستعمله مؤقتًا ثم يعيده."],["spelling","A2","Choose the correctly spelled word.",["necessary","neccessary","necesary","necessery"],0,"Necessary is spelled with one c and two s letters.","Necessary تُكتب بحرف c واحد وحرفي s."],["grammar","A2","We ___ to the museum last Saturday.",["went","go","have go","going"],0,"A finished time in the past takes the past simple.","وقت ماضٍ منتهٍ مثل last Saturday يتطلب الماضي البسيط."],["story","A2","Omar checked the weather, saw a storm warning, and moved the picnic indoors. What can we infer?",["He changed the plan to stay safe and dry.","He forgot where the picnic was.","The picnic had already ended.","He wanted to swim in the storm."],0,"He adapted the plan because the weather looked unsafe.","غيّر الخطة لأن حالة الطقس لم تكن مناسبة."],["listening","A2","“Could you tell me how to get to the station?” What is the speaker asking for?",["Directions","A job interview","A meal recommendation","A refund"],0,"The speaker wants directions to the station.","يطلب المتحدث إرشادات للوصول إلى المحطة."],["advanced","A2","In “The room was rather chilly,” chilly means ___.",["a little cold","extremely noisy","very crowded","brightly lit"],0,"Chilly means somewhat cold.","Chilly تعني باردًا بعض الشيء."],["vocabulary","B1","A “reliable” person is someone who ___.",["can be trusted","changes plans every minute","never listens","avoids all work"],0,"Reliable means dependable and trustworthy.","Reliable تعني جديرًا بالثقة ويمكن الاعتماد عليه."],["spelling","B1","Choose the correctly spelled word.",["accommodation","accomodation","acommodation","accommadation"],0,"Accommodation has double c and double m.","Accommodation تحتوي على حرفي c وحرفي m."],["grammar","B1","If she ___ earlier, she wouldn’t have missed the train.",["had left","left","would leave","has left"],0,"The third conditional uses past perfect in the if-clause.","يستخدم الشرط الثالث الماضي التام في جملة if."],["story","B1","A team misses its deadline, so its leader asks members to identify the bottleneck before setting a new schedule. What is the leader prioritising?",["Understanding the cause before planning again.","Blaming one person immediately.","Cancelling every future project.","Ignoring the delay."],0,"The leader wants to diagnose the problem before making a new plan.","يريد القائد تحديد سبب المشكلة قبل وضع خطة جديدة."],["listening","B1","“I see your point, but I’m not entirely convinced.” What does the speaker mean?",["They understand the argument but still have doubts.","They completely agree.","They did not hear anything.","They are changing the subject to travel."],0,"The speaker acknowledges the argument while expressing reservations.","يعترف المتحدث بوجاهة الرأي لكنه ما زال مترددًا."],["advanced","B1","Choose the closest meaning of “eventually”.",["in the end","immediately","by accident","for that reason"],0,"Eventually means in the end, after some time.","Eventually تعني في النهاية بعد مرور بعض الوقت."],["vocabulary","B2","A “tentative” conclusion is ___.",["provisional and open to change","certain beyond any doubt","unrelated to the evidence","deliberately dishonest"],0,"Tentative describes a conclusion that is not yet final or certain.","Tentative تصف نتيجة أولية غير نهائية وقابلة للتغيير."],["spelling","B2","Choose the correctly spelled word.",["conscientious","consciencious","conscientous","conscienctious"],0,"Conscientious is the standard spelling.","Conscientious هي التهجئة القياسية الصحيحة."],["grammar","B2","No sooner ___ the announcement than the audience began to applaud.",["had she finished","she had finished","did she finished","she finishes"],0,"No sooner at the beginning is followed by inversion with had.","عند بدء الجملة بـ No sooner نستخدم القلب مع had."],["story","B2","A journalist receives a dramatic claim from one source but waits for independent confirmation. Why?",["To avoid publishing an unverified claim.","To make the story less accurate.","To hide the source from every editor.","To ensure the claim is false."],0,"Independent confirmation improves reliability before publication.","التحقق المستقل يعزز موثوقية الخبر قبل نشره."],["listening","B2","“That proposal is not without merit, although its timing is questionable.” The speaker is ___.",["partly supportive but raises a concern","fully opposed to every aspect","certain the timing is perfect","unable to understand the proposal"],0,"“Not without merit” is a cautious positive assessment, followed by a reservation.","عبارة not without merit إيجابية بحذر، ثم يتبعها تحفظ."],["advanced","B2","“To qualify the claim” means to ___.",["make it more limited or precise","repeat it more loudly","prove it false automatically","remove all supporting evidence"],0,"To qualify a claim is to add limits or conditions to it.","تقييد الادعاء يعني إضافة حدود أو شروط تجعله أدق."],["vocabulary","C1","A “pervasive” influence is one that ___.",["spreads widely throughout something","appears only once","is easy to measure exactly","has no noticeable effect"],0,"Pervasive means spreading throughout or being present in many places.","Pervasive تعني منتشرًا على نطاق واسع."],["spelling","C1","Choose the correctly spelled word.",["idiosyncrasy","idiosyncracy","ideosyncrasy","idiosyncrasyy"],0,"Idiosyncrasy is the standard spelling.","Idiosyncrasy هي التهجئة الصحيحة."],["grammar","C1","Had the warning been taken seriously, the incident ___.",["might have been avoided","will be avoided","might avoid","would be avoiding"],0,"A past counterfactual result can use might have + past participle.","يمكن أن تأتي نتيجة الافتراض المخالف للماضي بصيغة might have والتصريف الثالث."],["story","C1","A researcher reports an unexpected result, then describes the sample limitations and calls for replication. What quality does this show?",["Methodological caution","Uncritical certainty","A refusal to present evidence","A desire to exaggerate findings"],0,"The researcher communicates findings while acknowledging limits and the need for verification.","يعرض الباحث النتائج مع الاعتراف بالحدود والحاجة إلى التحقق."],["listening","C1","“I would hesitate to characterise the outcome as a failure.” The speaker is ___.",["avoiding a categorical negative judgement","insisting it was unquestionably a failure","refusing to discuss the outcome","celebrating a complete success"],0,"The phrasing signals caution about applying the label “failure”.","الصياغة تدل على التحفظ قبل وصف النتيجة بالفشل."],["advanced","C1","“A cogent argument” is one that is ___.",["clear, logical, and persuasive","long but incoherent","based entirely on rumour","intentionally ambiguous"],0,"Cogent describes reasoning that is clear and convincing.","Cogent تصف حجة واضحة ومقنعة منطقيًا."],["vocabulary","C2","A “recondite” subject is ___.",["obscure and difficult to understand","widely known by everyone","simple to demonstrate","irrelevant by definition"],0,"Recondite means little known or requiring specialised knowledge.","Recondite تعني غامضًا أو يتطلب معرفة متخصصة."],["spelling","C2","Choose the correctly spelled word.",["inchoate","inchoate","inchote","inchoete"],0,"Inchoate is the standard spelling for something just beginning to form.","Inchoate هي التهجئة الصحيحة لشيء ما زال في طور التكوّن."],["grammar","C2","So compelling ___ that even its critics conceded the point.",["was the evidence","the evidence was","did the evidence","the evidence did"],0,"Fronted “so + adjective” can trigger subject–auxiliary inversion.","تقديم so مع الصفة قد يستلزم القلب بين الفاعل والفعل المساعد."],["story","C2","An analyst distinguishes what the data establishes from what it merely suggests, and explicitly notes competing explanations. What is the strongest description?",["The analyst is carefully separating evidence from inference.","The analyst is claiming the data proves everything.","The analyst is ignoring alternative explanations.","The analyst is avoiding any interpretation."],0,"The analyst distinguishes direct support from plausible interpretation.","يفصل المحلل بين ما تدعمه البيانات مباشرة وما يُستنتج منها."],["listening","C2","“That interpretation is tenable, though not uniquely compelled by the evidence.” What is implied?",["It is defensible, but other interpretations may also fit.","It is the only possible interpretation.","It has been conclusively disproved.","The evidence is entirely absent."],0,"Tenable means defensible; not uniquely compelled leaves room for alternatives.","Tenable تعني قابلًا للدفاع عنه، لكن الأدلة لا تفرضه كتفسير وحيد."],["advanced","C2","An “equivocal” statement is one that is ___.",["open to more than one interpretation","unambiguously precise","supported by a mathematical proof","entirely unrelated to context"],0,"Equivocal means ambiguous or open to different interpretations.","Equivocal تعني ملتبسًا وقابلًا لأكثر من تفسير."]];
